You're correct; the error is in the `+` operator you used to concatenate String variables inside the `System.out.println` call. In Java, you can't concatenate a String variable with an Integer directly. You need to insert the Integer into String format using `String.format()` or `+` with the variable as an argument (which works for `+`, but not for println if parsing fails).

The easiest fix is to use `String.format()` since it handles both integers and strings seamlessly.

